# Whole-workspace static gates, before anything leaves the machine.
#
# `pre-commit` runs `vp staged`, which lints and formats the files you touched. That is the
# right thing for a commit hook and it is structurally blind to the failure it cannot see:
# a change to file A that breaks file B, where B was never staged. Making `isGrouped` a
# required prop on `InfiniteCanvasWindowFrame` broke two test files that way on 2026-07-08,
# and nothing noticed for four hours, across six clean commits, because neither test was
# ever part of a commit.
#
# `vp check` type-checks the whole workspace in about four seconds. That is cheap enough to
# pay once per push and it closes the gap exactly.
#
# Tests and the build are deliberately not here. They belong in CI, where a red run costs
# nobody's attention mid-flow, and they are slow enough that a pre-push hook running them
# would get disabled within a week. This hook exists to catch the class of error that CI
# would otherwise be the *first* thing to notice.
#
# The dispatcher runs this under `sh -e`, so the first failing command aborts the push.
# `VITE_GIT_HOOKS=0 git push` skips it, if you must.

vp check

# The same four gates CI runs. All read source, need no build, and take milliseconds.
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-api-doc.mjs
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-pure-core.mjs
node packages/infinite-canvas/scripts/verify-api-stability.mjs
